Date: 2026-09-12
Drill: Podman Basics — Container Name Conflict & Fix

Commands:
- podman run -it --name alpine1 alpine
  -> Error: container name "alpine1" already in use
- podman ps
  -> No running containers listed
- podman rm -f alpine1
  -> alpine1 removed successfully
- podman run -it --name alpine1 alpine
  -> Container started, prompt shown: / #

Output:
Error: creating container storage: the container name "alpine1" is already in use...
CONTAINER ID  IMAGE       COMMAND     CREATED     STATUS      PORTS       NAMES
alpine1
/ #

Note:
This drill showed how Podman blocks reuse of container names if a stopped container still exists. Fix was to remove the old container with `podman rm -f alpine1`, then re‑run. Container launched successfully and gave interactive shell prompt.
